    {
      "title": "1. Calibrated trust and the trust–reliance distinction (Lee & See, 2004)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Trust = \"the attitude that an agent will help achieve an individual's goals",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "in a situation characterized by uncertainty and vulnerability.\" Reliance =",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the observable behavior that follows. Calibration = correspondence between",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "trust and the system's true capability.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Over-trust → over-reliance / misuse. Defers when it shouldn't.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Under-trust → under-reliance / disuse. Rejects help that would have worked.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The trust-calibration curve plots trust against true reliability; the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "diagonal is perfect calibration. Resolution = fine-grained trust that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "discriminates which cases the system handles well from those it doesn't (good",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "calibration on average can still have poor resolution). Calibration is a closed",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "loop, updated by performance feedback, disposition, and organizational norms.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Operator translation: don't ask \"do you trust the tool?\" Ask \"for which",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> decisions does it earn the follow?\" Coach for resolution, not blanket trust.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#1-calibrated-trust-and-the-trustreliance-distinction-lee-see-2004",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Automation bias & complacency (Parasuraman & Manzey, 2010)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "With an imperfect aid: commission errors (following a wrong automated",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "directive without cross-checking) and omission errors (missing what the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "automation failed to flag because you weren't monitoring). **Automation",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "complacency** is the attentional root - under load, monitoring drops. Appears in",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "experts and novices; not reliably removed by training; occurs in teams",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(redundancy can backfire via diffused responsibility); worsens with very high",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "automation reliability.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Operator translation: \"a human reviews it\" is a control only if it forces",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> engagement; under load it decays to rubber-stamping.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#2-automation-bias-complacency-parasuraman-manzey-2010",
          "note": null
