    {
      "title": "3. Algorithm aversion (Dietvorst et al., 2015)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "People abandon algorithms faster than humans after seeing them err, even",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "when the algorithm outperforms them. Error visibility is the trigger (seeing",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "it fail, not the failure rate). The 2018 follow-up: letting people **adjust the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "algorithm's output even slightly** restores willingness to use it (control lever).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Operator translation: a single visible miss can sink a net-better tool —",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> counter with adjustability, expectation-setting before the first error, and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> framing errors as bounded.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#3-algorithm-aversion-dietvorst-et-al-2015",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
