    {
      "title": "5. Why explanations & confidence displays often FAIL to calibrate reliance",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Plausible-but-wrong explanations increase over-reliance (Bansal et al.,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "2021, \"Does the Whole Exceed Its Parts?\"): explanations raised acceptance",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "whether the AI was right or wrong - agreement up, accuracy not.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Confidence helps only if calibrated; miscalibrated confidence degrades",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "decision quality, and displayed AI confidence shifts the human's own",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "self-confidence (anchoring uncertainty without improving ability).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Mechanism (dual-process): explanations feed the accept-heuristic rather",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "than interrupting it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Operator translation: \"we added explanations/confidence\" is not evidence of",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> appropriate reliance - verify behaviorally (does override-rate track",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/human-ai-interaction-psychology/#5-why-explanations-confidence-displays-often-fail-to-calibrate-reliance",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> error-rate?). Ship confidence numbers only if validated as calibrated.",
